{"segs": ["PA_ja_122:0.1"], "en": "Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_122:0.2", "PA_ja_122:0.3"], "en": "Ekakanipāta, Kusaṇāḷivagga (The Chapter on the Kusa Reed)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_122:0.4"], "en": "2. The Dummedha Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_122:1.1", "PA_ja_122:1.2"], "en": "“Having gained renown, the foolish man brings about his own ruin.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_122:1.3", "PA_ja_122:1.4"], "en": "\"He proceeds toward the harming of both himself and others.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_122:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the second Jātaka, the Dummedha-jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
